            <ArticleTitle>Clinical and radiological features of generalised lymphangiomatosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>402-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a paediatric patient who presented with fever, shortness of breath, and vague abdominal discomfort. Lesions removed surgically proved to be generalised lymphangiomatosis and were treated conservatively. The spectrum of abnormalities and radiological features are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
